# Core: the rules engine

## Never reference Godot

No `using Godot;`. No `Node`, `Vector2`, `Resource`, `GD.Print`, or any engine
type in a signature, field or local. This is not a style preference: CI builds
`WordRoguelike.Core.sln` on a bare .NET runner with no engine present, so an
engine reference here breaks the pipeline outright.

If a rule seems to need the engine, it belongs in `src/WordRoguelike.Game`, or
the dependency should be inverted behind an interface defined here.

## All randomness is injected and seeded

Never `new Random()`. Never `Guid.NewGuid()`, `DateTime.Now`, or
`Environment.TickCount` as a source of variation. RNG arrives as
`IRandomSource`.

Given the same seed and the same sequence of actions, a run must replay
identically. Reproducibility is what makes tests, replays, save files and a
future daily-challenge mode possible.

## Shape

- State is immutable records. Transitions are pure functions returning new state.
- Transitions return events describing what happened; callers animate from
  events rather than diffing state.
- Content (letter frequencies, score curves, reward tables) is data under
  `Content/`, not literals buried in logic.

## Strictness

Nullable is enabled and warnings are errors here. Do not suppress a warning to
get a build green; fix it, or justify the suppression in the PR. Public types
and non-obvious members need XML doc comments.

Add an abstraction when a second concrete case exists, not when you can imagine
one. No DI container, no MediatR, no repository pattern.
